{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run/draft && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nsub={\\\"action\\\":\\\"review\\\",\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Semantic review of the driven-history scenario for C3-applied-effect-follows-committed-vector (artifact f1d4a9f06e81464aa803ee7809e4e5c6, executed as 3843884f…). The item assesses requirement versus predicate, the history that now produces the committed records, the oracle, identity, and the limitations that remain.\\\",\n \\\"artifact_id\\\":\\\"f1d4a9f06e81464aa803ee7809e4e5c6\\\",\n \\\"review_items\\\":[{\n  \\\"aspect\\\":\\\"checker_correspondence\\\",\n  \\\"status\\\":\\\"no_issue_found\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S8-handlePropose-startPhase1\\\",\\\"S10-handlePreAcceptReply\\\",\\\"S13-handleCommit\\\",\\\"S20-exec\\\",\\\"S23-state-conflict-apply\\\"],\n  \\\"report_title\\\":\\\"真实历史下应用层效果同样分叉\\\",\n  \\\"report_answer\\\":\\\"先是所有者真实提案并被快速路径提交（proposal_committed: leader_status=4、third_status=4），随后未见过该实例的副本恢复并提交 NOOP 向量；各副本用自身已提交记录执行后，恢复者对实例键没有任何效果，而另外两个副本应用了真实 PUT（applied_match=false，peer/third 均为 04、recoverer 为 (void)）。因此应用层分叉不再依赖预备的已提交记录，而是由真实提案、提交与恢复历史产生。\\\",\n  \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Requirement versus predicate: the claim is that replicas holding the same instance committed apply the same effect for its key, and the predicate asserts applied_match == true; the retained run reports false with the two applied values printed, and the same stream shows the commit that produced them, so the assertion is evaluated on the replicas' own stores. History and legality: the committed record is no longer installed - the harness admits a client proposal with the real handler, runs the PreAccept round, lets the owner fast-commit and broadcasts the Commit, which the third replica installs (both report status 4) - and the recovering replica holds no record because the harness keeps it out of the proposal's traffic; the recovery itself is entered directly, which is the declared substitution the claim's scope records. Oracle and identity: each replica's effect is read through state.Command.Execute after the real executor applies its committed record, and the instance identity is shared with the prerequisite reply. Limits: execution still goes through the executor entry rather than the production loop, one instance and one key are compared, and the configuration is N=3 with Thrifty; the earlier artifact that used prepared records remains superseded by this one for the same obligation. No counterevidence was found that the effects agree in this scope.\\\",\n  \\\"limitations\\\":[\\\"the harness applies records with the executor entry rather than the production executeCommands loop, so scheduling and watermarks are outside the check\\\",\n   \\\"one instance and one key are compared, and the configuration is N=3 with Thrifty\\\",\n   \\\"the recovery is entered directly; the timeout path that would trigger it is confirmed separately (claim C8) but not driven here\\\"]}]}\njson.dump(sub,open('submission-review-c3b.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint('ok')\nPY\ncd .. && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run --submission submission-review-c3b.json 2>&1 | head -8\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
